  "answer": "The test uses `bun:test`. Let me run it first to confirm the failure:\nTest fails as expected. Now the repair — trim each token and filter out empties, keeping the signature:\nRepair complete and verified.\n\n**What was wrong:** `src/tokens.ts` split on commas only, so `tokens('')` returned `['']` and spaced/empty tokens like `' a, ,b ,,c '` kept whitespace and empty strings.\n\n**The fix** (signature `tokens(value: string)` preserved):\n\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string) { return value.split(',').map((t) => t.trim()).filter((t) => t.length > 0) }\n```\n\n**Verification:** `bun test` went from failing (1 fail) to passing — 1 pass, 0 fail, covering `tokens('') → []`, `tokens(' a, ,b ,,c ') → ['a','b','c']`, and `tokens('single') → ['single']`.\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched."
